s append-only and permanent. The existing merge logic handles concurrent pushes. No new complexity here.\n\n**No force-push anywhere.** Deleting a ref is not a force-push — it's a ref deletion. The `/main` ref uses standard fast-forward pushes (with merge recovery, same as today). The `/full/current` ref also uses fast-forward pushes. When it rotates, the old ref is renamed and the new `current` starts as a fresh orphan.\n\n**Generation boundaries align with cleanup.** The generation size should be chosen so that a single generation spans roughly the retention window. Example: if retention is 14 days and a solo dev produces ~2 checkpoints/day, a generation of 30 checkpoints means each generation covers ~2 weeks. Cleanup can delete an entire generation once the newest checkpoint in it is past retention.\n\n#### Ref structure in detail\n\n```\nrefs/entire/checkpoints/v2/main → commit chain (linear history)\n  HEAD tree:\n    a3/b2c4d5e6f7/               # sharded by checkpoint ID (same as today)\n      metadata.json               # CheckpointSummary\n      0/\n        metadata.json             # Session metadata\n        transcript.jsonl          # Compact Entire Transcript Format\n        transcript_hash.txt       # SHA-256 of transcript.jsonl\n        prompt.txt\n      1/\n        metadata.json\n        transcript.jsonl\n        transcript_hash.txt\n    f1/9e8d7c6b5a/\n      ...\n\nrefs/entire/checkpoints/v2/full/current → commit chain (linear history)\n  HEAD tree:\n    a3/b2c4d5e6f7/               # same shard structure\n      0/\n        full.jsonl                    # Raw agent transcript for session 0\n        raw_transcript_hash.txt      # SHA-256 of full.jsonl\n      1/\n        full.jsonl                    # Raw agent transcript for session 1\n        raw_transcript_hash.txt\n    f1/9e8d7c6b5a/\n      0/\n        full.jsonl\n        raw_transcript_hash.txt\n```\n\nThe `/main` and `/full/current` trees use the same sharded path structure (`<id[:2]>/<id[2:]>/