{"timestamp":"2026-04-30T22:01:45.748Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"exec_command_end","call_id":"call_rPP4OAkoMHiusferjDEmMVGn","process_id":"17465","turn_id":"019de066-a5e0-77f2-9c99-3236f9f7f1f1","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '214,452p' /Users/pfleidi/entire/company-knowledge/rfds/rfd-009-transcript-compaction.md"],"cwd":"/Users/pfleidi/entire/cli/.worktrees/fix/entire-migrate-checkpoint-order","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '214,452p' /Users/pfleidi/entire/company-knowledge/rfds/rfd-009-transcript-compaction.md","name":"rfd-009-transcript-compaction.md","path":"/Users/pfleidi/entire/company-knowledge/rfds/rfd-009-transcript-compaction.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","stdout":"","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"refs/entire/checkpoints/v2/main                ← permanent: metadata + compact transcripts\nrefs/entire/checkpoints/v2/full/current        ← active generation: raw logs (rotates when full)\nrefs/entire/checkpoints/v2/full/0000000000001  ← archived generation (deletable wholesale)\nrefs/entire/checkpoints/v2/full/0000000000002  ← archived generation (deletable wholesale)\n```\n\n**`/main`** is a single append-only ref with linear commit history. Works like today's `entire/checkpoints/v1` but stores only small, permanent data: `metadata.json`, `transcript.jsonl`, `transcript_hash.txt`, and `prompt.txt`. Deferred features such as persisted `assets/` blobs or pinned raw transcripts can be added later without changing the basic ref layout. `/main` never needs cleanup, grows slowly, and uses standard merge logic for concurrent pushes (same as today — the existing push-and-merge logic in `fetchAndMergeRef` works here).\n\n**`/full/current`** is a ref that accumulates raw `full.jsonl` files as commits. Each checkpoint adds its raw logs to this ref's tree using the same sharded layout (`<id[:2]>/<id[2:]>/0/full.jsonl`). When it reaches a configured capacity (e.g., N checkpoints or M megabytes), it rotates:\n\n1. Rename `current` → next sequential number (e.g., `0000000000001`)\n2. Create a fresh orphan `current`\n\n**`/full/NNNNNNNNNNNNN`** (archived generations) are frozen refs. Once all checkpoints in a generation age past the retention window, the entire ref is deleted — making the whole commit chain and all its raw log blobs unreachable in one operation.\n\n#### Why this works\n\n**Only 2-3 active refs at any time.** `/main` + `/full/current` + maybe one recent archived generation that hasn't been cleaned yet. Well within any hosting provider's limits, and invisible in the GitHub UI.\n\n**Cleanup = delete entire refs.** No tree surgery. No force-push. Just:\n```bash\ngit push origin --delete refs/entire/checkpoints/v2/full/0000000000001\n```\nThe entire commit chain becomes unreachable. Git GC reclaims all the large blobs. No need to understand the tree structure or modify individual files.\n\n**`/main` is never touched by cleanup.** It's append-only and permanent. The existing merge logic handles concurrent pushes. No new complexity here.\n\n**No force-push anywhere.** Deleting a ref is not a force-push — it's a ref deletion. The `/main` ref uses standard fast-forward pushes (with merge recovery, same as today). The `/full/current` ref also uses fast-forward pushes. When it rotates, the old ref is renamed and the new `current` starts as a fresh orphan.\n\n**Generation boundaries align with cleanup.** The generation size should be chosen so that a single generation spans roughly the retention window. Example: if retention is 14 days and a solo dev produces ~2 checkpoints/day, a generation of 30 checkpoints means each generation covers ~2 weeks. Cleanup can delete an entire generation once the newest checkpoint in it is past retention.\n\n#### Ref structure in detail\n\n```\nrefs/entire/checkpoints/v2/main → commit chain (linear history)\n  HEAD tree:\n    a3/b2c4d5e6f7/               # sharded by checkpoint ID (same as today)\n      metadata.json               # CheckpointSummary\n      0/\n        metadata.json             # Session metadata\n        transcript.jsonl          # Compact Entire Transcript Format\n        transcript_hash.txt       # SHA-256 of transcript.jsonl\n        prompt.txt\n      1/\n        metadata.json\n        transcript.jsonl\n        transcript_hash.txt\n    f1/9e8d7c6b5a/\n      ...\n\nrefs/entire/checkpoints/v2/full/current → commit chain (linear history)\n  HEAD tree:\n    a3/b2c4d5e6f7/               # same shard structure\n      0/\n        full.jsonl                    # Raw agent transcript for session 0\n        raw_transcript_hash.txt      # SHA-256 of full.jsonl\n      1/\n        full.jsonl                    # Raw agent transcript for session 1\n        raw_transcript_hash.txt\n    f1/9e8d7c6b5a/\n      0/\n        full.jsonl\n        raw_transcript_hash.txt\n```\n\nThe `/main` and `/full/current` trees use the same sharded path structure (`<id[:2]>/<id[2:]>/`). Given a checkpoint ID, the CLI/API knows exactly where to find data in both trees.\n\n#### Write path (CLI)\n\nAt condensation time, the CLI writes to two refs:\n\n```go\n// 1. Append metadata + compact transcript + transcript_hash to /main (same pattern as today)\nmainTree := spliceCheckpointSubtree(mainRootTree, checkpointID, mainEntries)\nmainCommit := createCommit(mainTree, mainParent, ...)\nSetReference(\"refs/entire/checkpoints/v2/main\", mainCommit)\n\n// 2. Append raw log + content_hash to /full/current\nfullTree := spliceCheckpointSubtree(fullRootTree, checkpointID, fullEntries)\nfullCommit := createCommit(fullTree, fullParent, ...)\nSetReference(\"refs/entire/checkpoints/v2/full/current\", fullCommit)\n\n// 3. Check if rotation is needed\nif generationSize(fullTree) >= maxCheckpointsPerGeneration {\n    rotate()  // rename current → next number, create fresh orphan curr…3791 chars truncated… ls-remote` to discover remote archived generation refs\n2. Fetch the latest archived generation (cheap — most blobs already local since we shared the same