son` is **only written at archive time** (when `/full/current` is rotated to a numbered ref), not on every write to `/full/current`. This ensures `/full/current` contains only sharded checkpoint directories, making tree merges during push recovery conflict-free.\n\nWhen `/full/current` reaches its capacity:\n\n```go\nfunc rotate() {\n    nextGen := nextGenerationNumber()  // e.g., \"0000000000001\"\n\n    // Write generation.json to the current tree before archiving\n    gen := computeGenerationTimestamps()  // derives oldest/newest from commit history\n    currentTree = addGenerationJSON(currentTree, gen)\n    currentCommit = createCommit(currentTree, currentParent, \"Archive generation\")\n    SetReference(\"refs/entire/checkpoints/v2/full/current\", currentCommit)\n\n    // Rename: current → numbered archive\n    archiveRef := fmt.Sprintf(\"refs/entire/checkpoints/v2/full/%s\", nextGen)\n    SetReference(archiveRef, currentCommit)\n\n    // Create fresh orphan current (empty tree, no parent)\n    emptyTree := buildEmptyTree()\n    newCommit := createCommit(emptyTree, nil, \"Start generation\")\n    SetReference(\"refs/entire/checkpoints/v2/full/current\", newCommit)\n}\n```\n\nThe generation number is zero-padded for lexicographic sorting. The next generation number is derived from existing archived ref names.\n\n#### Generation sizing\n\nThe generation size controls the tradeoff between cleanup granularity and overhead:\n\n| Generation size | Cleanup granularity | Overhead |\n|----------------|-------------------|----------|\n| Small (10 checkpoints) | Fine — can delete soon after retention | More generations, more archived refs |\n| Large (500 checkpoints) | Coarse — must wait for all 500 to age out | Fewer refs, but delays space reclamation |\n\n**Recommended default: ~100 checkpoints per generation.** For a solo dev doing ~2 checkpoints/day, this spans ~50 days — well past a 14-day retention window, so cleanup can delete a generation within weeks of its oldest checkpoint aging out. For a team of 5, a generation fills in ~10 days, giving even finer cleanup granularity.\n\nGeneration metadata (`generation.json`) is written to the tree root at archive time only — not during normal writes to `/full/current`. This keeps `/full/current` free of root-level files, ensuring conflict-free tree merges during push recovery. The cleanup tool reads `generation.json` from archived generations to assess eligibility without walking the full tree.\n\n#### Cleanup path\n\n```\n1. List archived generation refs: entire/checkpoints/v2/full/NNNNN...\n2. For each generation, read generation.json → check newest_checkpoint_at\n3. If newest checkpoint is older than RETENTION_DAYS:\n   a. Optionally archive to cold storage\n   b. Delete the ref: git push origin --delete entire/checkpoints/v2/full/0000000000001\n4. Done — entire commit chain becomes unreachable, GC reclaims blobs\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":3667},"formatted_output":"","status":"completed"}}
